{"skill":{"slug":"zoho-calendar","displayName":"zoho-calendar"},"version":{"version":"1.2.5","createdAt":1790941376035,"changelog":"Simplify the login instructions to the code flow (maton login prints a link; finish with maton login --code <CODE>), drop the API Key subsection, and pin the Maton CLI install to 0.4.0.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":56206,"sha256":"996dcdf4aa2fde39ab32e6c0e04458033a17775b5028af9cf089534ff5f721ab","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/calendly/triggers.md","size":10281,"sha256":"ae92dbfb6dd4caf628900b293d1b3c6e7d5e70cf7f6a9397407594daf50d4a48","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/github/triggers.md","size":61142,"sha256":"7424d3be38ec400eb8a4b0a6a94a94eeec40208c0bcee29a61caa5da48eea7f4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/google-mail/triggers.md","size":2648,"sha256":"5cc5065cd7db33dc33715675bbb0ee29ed49657ad9ad4354aebd1a9efdf8d8f3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/hubspot/triggers.md","size":8298,"sha256":"439d56e4d02e119e1de3caf79a0334243ae70c583a3e15847831c396f39c2837","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/linear/triggers.md","size":7270,"sha256":"641f6496f50e09faab921ef4c06f725122b798cb034e9f0dfaf9f838074ab377","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/notion/triggers.md","size":5840,"sha256":"fdaf3840d8213dbd7549426c1166f94cc94b09e022a1611ef2dad6f36db2f969","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/slack/triggers.md","size":6181,"sha256":"b5ee099a215223a7e5186c41a0d13fc1de68e977719304c509df105843d81f38","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/stripe/triggers.md","size":25651,"sha256":"ae091545396a376c7ecfe09e94b46b7bbb44fd8a72ea954bcc1239052b7959f0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/time/triggers.md","size":1140,"sha256":"b8f5a523501f8d03e11e58f6426cd96b54ba0c66c8983b57c0ea31386b309e01","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2429,"sha256":"6fed147c115699f6988c5d216709c01f3fbecc15976cfba85d680a0bc681d145","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1790941771196,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4ddffcffd42c1ac6a4d6d0f665c1f83604c7834c7fe4dabca92f16d19404043c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4ddffcffd42c1ac6a4d6d0f665c1f83604c7834c7fe4dabca92f16d19404043c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790941614395},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":18,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1790941771196},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This Zoho Calendar skill is broad and includes automation reference material, but its sensitive behaviors are disclosed, scoped, and tied to user approval.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, OAuth login, OS credential-store use, and a raw API-key fallback are proportionate for a hosted API integration, and the artifact instructs agents not to inspect, export, log, or persist credentials.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation is a documented Maton CLI install through pinned npm/Homebrew instructions; the artifact itself is Markdown reference material and ships no executable scripts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package includes shared trigger catalog references for other apps such as Gmail and Linear, but the main skill and each reference file explicitly state that those files do not widen Zoho Calendar capability and should only be used when the user asks for that source by name.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"OAuth tokens, hosted functions, triggers, destinations, and watch checkpoints can persist beyond a single call, but the skill describes those flows plainly, prefers DENY_ALL network policy, requires separate approval for writes and automations, and warns about persistent data forwarding.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill supports Zoho Calendar read/write/delete operations plus optional Maton-hosted functions and triggers; these are high-impact capabilities but they match the stated calendar and scheduling purpose and are repeatedly gated on user confirmation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Before installing, understand that this skill can manage and delete Zoho Calendar data through your Maton-connected account and can set up persistent functions or triggers if you approve them. Use read-only actions first, confirm every write/delete/automation, keep trigger destinations on Maton-controlled hosts unless you explicitly trust another host, and do not expose Maton API keys or OAuth credentials.","findings":"[SDI-2] expected: The Gmail trigger file is not core Zoho Calendar functionality, but the artifact explicitly identifies it as shared platform event-source reference text, says it does not widen the skill, and warns about private mail forwarding and destination approval.\n[SDI-1] expected: The Linear trigger file is likewise shared platform reference material; it is disclosed in the main skill, marked non-operative for Zoho Calendar on its own, and includes scoping and sensitive-data cautions rather than hidden automation instructions.\n[aig-skill-scan] expected: The static scan reported no security findings, which is consistent with the inspected Markdown-only artifact and the absence of embedded executable code.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1790941771196}}}}}